			<div class="content" id="post-content-4841151">
									

<p>Can you, a normal foundation agent who has just been promoted, save humanity? If so&#8230; how many times and at what cost?</p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article, Tale, Site Dossier, Other (It is a combination of all the previous ones using a hub page)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The O5 council creates a new staff classification with O5 security clearance that works under direct orders of the O5 to allow them to have more staff at their disposal for operations that couldn't be told about to those with a lower security level. An agent at the Foundation is promoted to this new staff designation and is assigned to watch over an O5 level security project designed to stop end of the world scenarios from happening.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> In light of several new SCP discoveries that could lead to end of the world scenarios the O5 council decides that methods need to be made for dealing with problems like these, so they make a new project and promote the most reliable agent they have to a recently made position which grants him O5 level clearance. He’s assigned to spearhead the project, creating his own team and coming up with methods to then test and hopefully find the best method to deal with every SCP object or threat, reporting everything he’s doing directly to the council. There will be SCP’s referenced and it will also include several that I’m coming up with. As the agent continues coming up with new methods he starts compiling journals of those involved in the testing of those methods as well as the journals of those who were under the effects by the objects before the methods were tested, revealing to him how much sacrifice they will have to make and have been making to move forward.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I think that the incorporation of an character who is overseeing the files being the one who you are in the perspective of is pretty unique and different from other things on the site as they mostly don’t give the reader a character.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I have not nearly finished yet so I won't be posting the sandbox pages very soon as there is still a lot to figure out in terms of the story. I just want to know if the concept is good enough that I should continue it and I want to get greenlit earlier on so I don’t have to worry about it later, I’m not sure if this will need to be split into several drafts since the pages will inevitably have cross links to each other in them</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

