<p>Hello, ok so I see what your going for here but I don't think there's enough happening here and, what I mean by that is your missing the big so what. Like you have this guy that takes up a position to stop end of the world events but thats it. How are you going to keep this story interesting to the reader. What I suggest adding is the big so what. There doesn't have to be a moral or anything but just what do you want the reader to take away or understand from this piece. For example SCP-3008 uses the journals of the people stuck in the SCP to allow the reader to connect and feel bad and scared for the people trapped there. How do you want your reader to connect to this scp. Is it about the life and death situations the O5s have to make? is it about the hardship of working at the foundation what is you base theme?</p>
<p>Hope this helps PM me if you want follow up.</p>

