<p>I think the ending will be kind of ambiguous and I haven’t fully planned it out yet, but it will include the agent finding out something that he wasn’t expected to be able to, and as the project starts seeing results he stops it with his final journal entry being a rambling mess talking about the Foundation, the O5, the Administrators , and other things that aren’t known pieces of the Foundation, with the entry ending with “How could I be so naive? All these lies right from the beginning&#8230; all those people dead for nothing&#8230; and I feel nothing&#8230; I'm exactly the monster they wanted.” With a personnel update log after that showing that the project has been assigned to a different staff member by the agent (something he should not have the power to do) and is in the process of being continued, and that the agent has been promoted again to a position that isn’t mentioned anywhere in the Foundation’s database except in his final entry. Ultimately what he finds out is something about the Foundation that makes him qualified to be in a position that isn’t even mentioned on the database, at which point he himself continues the project, assigning someone else to take his place as the person running it, all of which has just happened in the universe so what comes next is a mystery.</p>

