														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4841827">
									

<p>I think that he discovers the existence and history of the position that i already mentioned he is moved up to, which leads him to know as much about the Foundation as the O5 council themselves, within this information he finds out that the entirety of the Hinterland Division that he sacrificed so much for was based upon lies, namely lies about the actual existence of several of the world threat entities that he was working to stop, which were made up from the beginning, the explanation behind this being to &quot;Convince him that he is capable of stopping them with fakes, throw in some carnage, tactically get rid of expendables, come up with any backstories you need, we need him to think that he is a capable leader saving the world. Once that's done he'll be psychologically ready to handle the real Hinterland Division.&quot; after this he discovered that there are actual world threats that he is expected to deal with. The ones that he had already beaten, needing to sacrifice countless lives and abandon his morals to do so, having been a test run, threats designed by the Foundation to challenge his abilities and turn him into the candidate required, the problem is that all of the things that he did to deal with those threats was real, and the O5 had let him continue, knowing that if they stepped in it would ruin the plan. So basically he discovers that the Foundation willingly allowed hundreds of personnel and innocents, even children to be hurt, tortured, and killed in order to save humanity. What scared him was not that the foundation did this, he knew they would do anything to protect humanity, and this was definitely to protect humanity, he was scared because he realized the plan worked, and he himself had changed and no longer cared about those peoples lives, and was now ready to sacrifice everything to the Foundation.</p>

