			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843331">
									

<p>Okay so let me try to explain it a little bit better since my original post was kind of vague. The division technically already existed and has been a key part of the foundation since not long after the Foundations conception, and has already eliminated several threats. The foundation isn’t really making a new division this is just a story behind the creation of the newest iteration of its leader. The reason that the other divisions of the foundation are not sufficient at it is because the threats that the division is made to stop are those that require entire knowledge of the foundation and it’s recourses , regardless of the security needed to have that information. The main idea of the story is very much inspired by the book Enders Game, I’m not sure if you’ve read it. The idea is that the existing Hinterland division is failing because it has not had someone fulfilling the position of the leader and strategist in years, as no good candidates have been found, and without someone that has the prowess to spearhead the division the researchers and members in the division are struggling to do it. The agent that the O5 chooses is purposefully trained and manipulated into being the best possible person to continue the work of the division. This story isn’t really meant to create a new part of the foundation but to explore an existing part of it that has been in my head for a really long time but is not included in any records due to the importance of its mission making its secrecy extremely important as well. I really want to shed some light and provide a look into what’s behind the curtain of the foundation since once you reach the level of the O5 and their staff everything gets rather hazy. The main character is of course the most explored and shown character but he also has several people he knows within the foundation, and I plan to actually develop the character at least partially of one of the O5 members, the one that is currently fulfilling the role of O5-13. There are going to be tales that show characters a low in the foundation of D class personnel in all of this as well. Of course I’m probably not going to write everything about this idea I’m coming up with as this is technically part of an even larger story about how the foundation has been changing and events within it over the years, this is just my version of a snippet of the mysteries in the ever mysterious organization.</p>

